Here is a CSS class to center content both horizontally and vertically on the page:

```css
.centered-content {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
  margin: 0;
}
```

**How it works:**
*   `display: flex`: Enables Flexbox layout.
*   `justify-content: center`: Centers the content horizontally.
*   `align-items: center`: Centers the content vertically.
*   `min-height: 100vh`: Ensures the container takes up at least the full height of the viewport.
*   `margin: 0`: Removes default body margins that might push content down.

