Here is the edited program. I have included the `<cmath>` header and used the `std::sqrt` function. Note that since the input is an integer, the result is cast to an integer for printing, though you might want to use `double` for the input if you need decimal precision.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <cmath> // Required for std::sqrt

int main() 
{ 
    int number; 

    std::cout << "Enter an integer: "; 
    std::cin >> number; 

    // Add code to print square root of the number
    // Casting to int to match the input type, or use double for decimal precision
    int squareRoot = static_cast<int>(std::sqrt(number)); 

    std::cout << "The square root of " << number << " is " << squareRoot << std::endl; 

    return 0;
}
```

